et. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices, an edge’s index being its rank"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"count per 64-bit word, and a rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices, except one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that keeps every vertex, which keeps the base’s rows and edge indices."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The view holds a copy of the base, so mutating the original doesn’t show through. The base","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must have vertex indices; construction traps when ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a "},{"code":"GraphAdaptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", its generation is the base’s, and it reads the base’s attached maps."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"[map, of: vertex]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"[map, ofEdgeAt: position]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" trap for a vertex or an edge the view drops,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and their "},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" forms throw. "},{"code":"values(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the base’s, by the base’s positions. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm on the view reads it only at the kept edges."}]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphAdaptor","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checked:)-2n5fj","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checked:)-34kf9","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checkedEdgeAt:)-40a5z","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checkedEdgeAt:)-7lnri","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:of:)-16yvl","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:of:)-3uhp3","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:ofEdgeAt:)-1tf